Notebook[{
Cell["Unit 1 \[CenterDot] Reading a Sequence, Writing a Sequence", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c41630e8-2673-49e4-91ec-7db93abc6036"],

Cell["\<\
Deep LSTMs as encoder and decoder (Sutskever, Vinyals and Le, 2014) \
\[LongDash] TensorNets units of learning, 1 of 4\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"fcb42de3-7cbf-40a7-adff-40a7463f349c"],

Cell["\[Copyright] 2026 Computational Classnotes \[CenterDot] CC BY-NC-SA \
4.0", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"81bea77d-bb8d-4007-b54e-3bfc527b76de"],

Cell["\<\
A translator can be two recurrent networks: one reads the whole sentence into \
a fixed-size vector, the other writes the translation from it. This unit \
builds that machine from plain arrays, one part per section, and checks each \
part against Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s own layers. Evaluate the notebook \
from top to bottom; every section ends with a check that returns True or a \
number quoted in the write-up \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Unit 1 \[CenterDot] \
Reading a Sequence, Writing a Sequence\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], which has the \
same section numbers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f80d64a6-dbc5-48e0-8bd8-c89eb6c39427"],

Cell["\<\
Before you start: choose Evaluation \[RightPointer] Quit Kernel \
\[RightPointer] Local, so no definitions from other notebooks interfere. The \
whole unit evaluates in under a minute.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c58d331-1b7f-4172-bad0-f78f5f3bd0da"],

Cell["1. Toolkit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"38bdbf33-0f3a-417b-942e-03980c883738"],

Cell["\<\
Every function the unit uses, in one cell. \[Sigma] is the logistic function. \
lstmStep is one step of an LSTM, written from its four gate equations (\
\[Section]3). lstmRun runs it over a sequence, deepRun stacks several LSTMs (\
\[Section]4), decodeStep is one step of the decoder (\[Section]5). withStates \
gives a Wolfram LSTM layer its starting states as inputs. clipNorm, rate and \
beam are the training and decoding recipes of \[Section]7 and \[Section]8.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9d44283b-c5ff-4ec5-a6a0-60910ddf3e47"],

