Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Fig. 1. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11]],
 "The encoder\[Dash]decoder. The encoder reads the reversed source and ends \
in the thought vector v; the decoder starts from v and writes the target, one \
word per step, reading back the word it has just written."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21a76529-55d8-48ff-b9e1-97487b7020e1"],

Cell["3. The LSTM cell", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1941fc0a-2c5d-4dfc-a20b-458fa72a1728"],

Cell["\<\
An LSTM keeps two vectors: the hidden state h, which it shows to the next \
layer, and the memory cell c, which it keeps for itself. At each step it \
reads an input x and computes four gates from x and the previous h. Each gate \
is a number between 0 and 1 per cell, except g, the new content, which is \
between \[Minus]1 and 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cbc7898d-be0e-4f12-b3aa-c4d51604aa80"],

Cell["\<\
i = \[Sigma](W_i x + U_i h + b_i)    f = \[Sigma](W_f x + U_f h + b_f)    o = \
\[Sigma](W_o x + U_o h + b_o)    g = tanh(W_g x + U_g h + b_g)\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"5d88ac06-0127-4612-bf41-067ba8100c8f"],

Cell["c\[Prime] = f c + i g        h\[Prime] = o tanh(c\[Prime])", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"3d311ed5-15c7-4861-b0cc-b2c6cc368c0b"],

Cell["\<\
i decides how much new content to write, f how much old memory to keep, o how \
much of the memory to show. The memory is updated by addition, not by \
repeated multiplication with a weight matrix, which is what lets information \
and gradients survive over long sentences.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7de29f2-fabc-4c80-9134-f785df21a930"],

Cell["3.1 Worked by hand: one step of a one-cell LSTM", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"e246e2ad-89ea-4f7b-a2c4-a87f73cdd9ff"],

Cell["\<\
Take one input and one cell, every weight 0.5 and every bias 0, start from h \
= c = 0 and read x = 1. Every gate sees 0.5 \[CenterDot] 1 + 0.5 \[CenterDot] \
0 + 0 = 0.5. So i = f = o = \[Sigma](0.5) = 1/(1 + e^\[Minus]0.5) = 0.6225, \
and g = tanh(0.5) = 0.4621. The memory becomes c\[Prime] = 0.6225 \
\[CenterDot] 0 + 0.6225 \[CenterDot] 0.4621 = 0.2877. The output is h\[Prime] \
= 0.6225 \[CenterDot] tanh(0.2877) = 0.6225 \[CenterDot] 0.2800 = 0.1743.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"9033d4e4-a6e4-46bc-8381-1cbbd0ebdfed"],

