      RowBox[{"10", "^", 
       RowBox[{"-", "5"}]}]}]}], "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eb064f79-89f1-42e6-8313-f60d019e33e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[10]=",ExpressionUUID->"c497146c-a74e-4a13-97a2-154c8a66d8cc"],

Cell["\<\
Check: {True, True, True}. The next-word distribution over 10 words is a \
probability distribution, and the decoder\[CloseCurlyQuote]s first layer, \
started from the encoder\[CloseCurlyQuote]s states, agrees with Wolfram\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s layer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d7c24173-a949-4b5a-a496-54565b21fc1c"],

Cell["\<\
During training the decoder reads the correct previous word, not its own \
guess (teacher forcing). At test time it reads its own output, and beam \
search (\[Section]8) chooses which outputs to keep.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c787e053-e359-4cf0-afdb-975c3cc5eac2"],

Cell["6. Reversing the source", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f81d65e-5693-4528-a20c-3f5600e49e88"],

Cell["\<\
Feed the source reversed: c, b, a instead of a, b, c, while the target stays \
\[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Gamma]. Nothing else changes, yet the paper\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s test BLEU rose from 25.9 to 30.6 (Section 3.3). The \
reason is distance. Put the source at positions 1\[Ellipsis]T and the target \
after it at T + 1\[Ellipsis]2T, with word i of the target aligned to word i \
of the source.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"88fdf084-b4f0-49c5-acc5-e1f7c3b89eba"],

Cell["6.1 Worked by hand: T = 3", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"6feca2fe-50c0-40c2-8c07-8a6bf2aaa3bb"],

Cell["\<\
Forward: a, b, c sit at 1, 2, 3 and \[Alpha], \[Beta], \[Gamma] at 4, 5, 6. \
Each pair is 3 apart: 4 \[Minus] 1 = 5 \[Minus] 2 = 6 \[Minus] 3 = 3. \
Reversed: c, b, a sit at 1, 2, 3, so a is at 3, b at 2, c at 1. The gaps are \
4 \[Minus] 3 = 1, 5 \[Minus] 2 = 3, 6 \[Minus] 1 = 5. The average is 3 both \
ways, but the first pair is now only 1 step apart, so the network can link a \
to \[Alpha] at once and build from there.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"39817dca-15cf-444d-834d-06a84457c398"],

