Cell["\<\
Check: {{1.}, True}. Plain NetInitialize leaves every forget-gate bias at 1; \
after uniformInit every parameter of the two-layer LSTM is within \
\[PlusMinus]0.08.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2cc8a5f-7d24-4aeb-8af6-4615ca6648fa"],

Cell["7.2 Clipping the gradient by its norm", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"671f05c8-9e8c-4a08-898b-9a2f884935f3"],

Cell["\<\
LSTMs rarely suffer from vanishing gradients but can suffer from exploding \
ones. For each batch the paper computes the norm s of the whole gradient g, \
all parameters together, and if s > 5 rescales g to 5g/s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd59b29e-63ae-4d55-aa6c-42730adbaa7a"],

Cell["s = \:2016g\:2016\:2082 ;   if s > 5 :  g \[LeftArrow] 5 g / s", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"ec6946f5-685b-44a1-b7ec-b775a7a84c3e"],

Cell["\<\
Let g = (6, 8). Its norm is \[Sqrt](36 + 64) = 10 > 5, so g becomes (6, 8) \
\[CenterDot] 5/10 = (3, 4), whose norm is 5. The direction is unchanged. \
Clamping each component to \[PlusMinus]5 instead would give (5, 5), which \
points somewhere else.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"8223a0ee-565a-4860-835e-7b83cae524d4"],

