Cell["\<\
Check: {True, 384112000}. The formula agrees with Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s \
own count for a small layer, and the total is the paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c209e51-aa1e-47c8-bdae-55e59c50d3a7"],

Cell["10. Exercises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d281b934-a8bd-4667-b4bc-0798b6701ba2"],

Cell["\<\
1. Repeat the hand computation of \[Section]3.1 with x = \[Minus]1. Which \
gates change, and why does h\[Prime] come out negative?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ef18283-eb8c-4931-904c-9ef3ca01f890"],

Cell["\<\
2. For a source of length T = 10, list the forward and reversed distances of \
\[Section]6 and their averages.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b691fcd9-9d11-4427-9e3b-316f73aa02ab"],

Cell["3. What is the learning rate at epoch 6.2?", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04136e12-426d-472f-a39c-d0492b5c3799"],

Cell["\<\
4. How many parameters has a two-layer LSTM with 256 inputs and 512 cells per \
layer? Check your answer against Wolfram\[CloseCurlyQuote]s count.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4baaa314-d0de-41dd-b083-1a8426c304bd"],

Cell["\<\
5. In the toy model of \[Section]8, change the probability of <e> after A \
from 0.4 to 0.7. Does greedy decoding still lose?\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4fed108b-ea76-4321-89ff-d11285a564c0"],

Cell["Answers, computed:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"abb3eb86-69e9-446c-b07e-c2eb785a7e9e"],

