Cell["\<\
1: every gate sees \[Minus]0.5, so i = f = o = \[Sigma](\[Minus]0.5) = 0.3775 \
and g = tanh(\[Minus]0.5) = \[Minus]0.4621; the new content is negative, so c\
\[Prime] and h\[Prime] are negative. 4: 3 674 112 both ways. 5: no; greedy \
now finds A<e> with 0.6 \[Times] 0.7 = 0.42, which beats B<e> with 0.38.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ebdd8463-e681-4479-a6f1-a536580be72a"],

Cell["11. Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f290f952-de3f-4fdb-a2bb-f047457cf7a6"],

Cell["\<\
Two deep LSTMs translate: one reads the whole source into the final states of \
its layers, the other writes from them, one word at a time. The LSTM\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s additive memory, controlled by its forget gate, carries \
information across the sentence. Reversing the source puts the first words \
next to each other. Small starting weights, clipping the gradient by its norm \
and a halving learning rate make training reliable, and a narrow beam finds \
better outputs than greedy decoding.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a28adec-fec7-48c1-a655-50172e5bd068"],

Cell["\<\
Next: Unit 2 turns mathematics into sequences that such a machine can learn \
from, and Unit 3 replaces the LSTM with attention.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ce717f1-fdd7-4461-a7ac-968981b913b2"],

Cell["\[Copyright] 2026 Computational Classnotes \[CenterDot] CC BY-NC-SA \
4.0", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2b261704-bf92-4b4d-803d-7b71227855eb"]
},
